[node name="SouthWall" type="Node2D" parent="Objects/Boundary"]
editor_description = "South boundary road wall (Milestone G Batch 2). Production RedBrickWall3m modules exactly 96 px apart (Wall01..Wall37 at local x 48 + 96k) with a RedBrickVerandaPier pilaster on every join and both free ends (Pier00..Pier37 at local x 96k); piers come after the walls so they draw on top at equal Y. Origin = west end of the run on the wall line (world -1250, 1400): the run spans world x -1250..2302 on the blockout line y 1400 (north edge of the sidewalk), from the Main Gate tower's east face (MainGateLandmark/Tower, local x +140; Pier00 sits half behind it) to under PrototypeEdgeEast. Basis: whole view.png / field.jpg / tennis+futsal court.png show one continuous low red-brick wall along the road (banners on the road side, tree band inside); mainGate.jpg gives the brick and coping language; pilasters about every 3 m per the user. Approximate: height and coping are fixed by the generated modules (2.4 m wall, 2.8 m pier), the line and start come from the blockout, the east end is a prototype limit (the real wall continues); banners are not built. RunCollision (one rectangle at the pier footprint depth) gives one smooth stop line; ShadowOccluder (light mask 1) replaces the blockout's generated occluder because the generated props have none. To extend: duplicate the last wall and pier (with their ContactShadow) and add 96 to x, then widen RunCollision/Shape and ShadowOccluder by 96 (see Docs/CAMPUS_MAP.md)."
y_sort_enabled = true
position = Vector2(-1250, 1400)

